    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "again, I'm Marvin Alny, and this is Which Way LA, KCRW's ongoing series on the issues Southern Californians care about. Kamala Harris won the race for State Attorney General last month by a fraction of one point, but she's already a national celebrity. The New York Times says she's one of 17 women with a chance of being president. But how many Southern Californians know what she stands for? We'll talk with her about her background, her priorities, and her ambitions. Also tonight, the Ninth Circuit Court of Appeals heard arguments today on Proposition 8. Will the court reverse the judge who called a ban on gay marriage unconstitutional? Later on, holiday shopping, China, and economic recovery. First, here's the news. Warming only back with which way LA on KCRW, Black Friday and Cyber Monday were a lot more active than a lot of people expected. What are the early indicators from holiday shopping and what do shopping habits in China have to do with US economic recovery? First, California's ban on same-sex marriage. Prop 8 was declared unconstitutional by a federal judge, and today the Ninth Circuit Court of Appeals took up the case. Neither Attorney General Jerry Brown nor Governor Schwarzenegger was willing to defend it in court. Douglas Neejame is Professor of Law at Loyola Law School, and it's good to have you on our program.",
