    "turn_idx": 51,
    "turn_text": "well i i know each of them and have worked with them on one level or another professionally i had part of the i think that the significance of those uh... Of those leaders in being part of this transition is to also highlight a point that I often make because I believe it to be true, which is that these issues are mostly nonpartisan. They're not even bipartisan. They're just nonpartisan. And we have to approach the solution and a quest for solutions to problems in a way that realizes that we cannot afford to just be mired in ideology, and instead we should just focus on what are practical outcomes and solutions. As a career prosecutor, I have never known a robber to approach his victim and ask, what is their political affiliation? When we talk about what we need to do to fix America's prison system crisis, and in particular, highlighted in California, I would suggest to you that focusing on re-entering former offenders by getting them education and job training and parenting skills is not an ideological perspective. It's a practical perspective because if we don't do that, they are going to re-offend and cost us so much more money. On an annual basis, for example, you can look at what we pay into California's criminal justice system and it varies, it ranges from about $10 billion to $25 billion a year in a system that is broken.",
