    "turn_text": "So reentry is a relatively new criminal justice concept. And it is about a focus on the reentering former offender. So for example, Warren, the average prison sentence in California is only 24 months. That's the average prison sentence. So that tells us two things about what's going on in the prison system in California and our criminal justice system by extension. The average person being sentenced is not being sentenced for that most atrocious, horrible, violent crime that we see on television on every night on some, you know, movie. Because 24 months is not that sentence. That's going to be 10, 15, 25 to life. So the average prison sentence, prison being sentenced, is not being sentenced for that horrendous violent crime. But the second piece of it is that the 24-month sentence, average sentence, tells you they're all coming out. And",
