    "turn_idx": 94,
    "turn_text": "Warren, optimism is key, and I'm going to tell you why you and I should both be optimists about this. Two years ago, knowing exactly what you are talking about needed to be done, I approached Karen Bass, then speaker, now Congresswoman, and together she and I worked on a bill that is called the Back on Track Reentry Act, and it was modeled after the reentry initiative I created in San Francisco. We took it up to Sacramento. It passed. Governor Schwarzenegger signed it into law. And as of January of 2010, the Back on Track Reentry Act of California is now in California's penal code, in the penal code. And so I think there's more work that can be done legislative in nature to help facilitate more reentry work. But the work has started. And that's why I'm so excited about The service that I can hopefully provide at the Attorney General of California on this issue as well as many others. I think there's a lot of room for work and I think that also, again, in crisis we should see that there are also great opportunities and with the budget crisis we have in California right now I think we have a lot of opportunities for everyone to say just fix it. I'm going to put ideology aside, just fix the darn thing. And that's where these initiatives come into",
