    "turn_idx": 118,
    "turn_text": "Cyber Monday was huge this year. It was the first year we saw spending top $1 billion online. It's basically the single biggest day of online shopping that we've had. And that hasn't been hugely surprising to the analyst. Deloitte was expecting that online sales were going to go up about 15% this year overall. And the Cyber Monday sales is up about 16% compared with last year. So pretty significant shift. But I think that's really reflective of that more people are looking to shop online in general. We also saw a lot more retailers offering great deals over Black Friday weekend this year. You could get the doorbusters online without having to wait in those crazy lines and stores.",
