    "turn_idx": 130,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's a little hard right now to determine how much of this is really, you know, people wanting to spend more versus what we're hearing from some analysts is that there is pent up demand. People we were hearing even for back to school this year, they're replacing their computers, they're buying things that they haven't bought for the past three years. It's not that they really have that free money to spend, just that they haven't spent it in three years. The money is burning a hole in their pockets and they feel the need to upgrade certain things. uh... certainly other consumers are certain are feeling more confident and that's showing up in those those statistics with more people saying they're going to buy jewelry they're going to buy some smaller gifts for themselves and overall they're not watching their wallet as much as they have been",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_09",
