    "turn_text": "Well, it's a significant drag. I mean, the 2000s boom, the engine behind that, That boom was, to a large extent, people buying homes, borrowing money, which boosted the financial industry, and then taking loans out on their homes to consume more than they made. It was a huge part of the engine that grew the 2000s bubble. And it's going to be difficult to achieve that same rate of growth without some other engine.",
