    "turn_text": "Well, they had to really start the sales early this year. They were worried about inventory and we saw a lot of early deals. And once one of your competitors offers it, then the rest of the stores have to follow suit or they see that consumers are not going to be shopping with them at all. And there are a few tricks that they use to really get the consumer in the store and potentially inflate the discount because consumers are very discount driven. We're trained to look for those big numbers and not necessarily evaluate the underlying price. So we'll see what the retailers end up doing in the next couple of weeks. Usually this week and specifically this Monday, two weeks before Christmas, tends to be a pretty big online shopping day in previous years. So we'll see what happens today in the next couple of days.",
