  {
    "episode_id": 89389,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89389.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 157,
    "turn_text": "You know, usually, I think historically, it's sort of bobbed around between 16, 70 percent. I mean, generally, when you look back on the boom years between, say, 2004, 2007, I mean, this was a bubble that we were talking about. We're probably looking at a period of American history. in which we had overconsumption. We had people spending more than they were earning and saving rates down into the near zero and then even a negative for some quintiles in America. So",
