  {
    "episode_id": 89389,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89389.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 159,
    "turn_text": "want to go back to that point. We want to find more stable sources of growth. That's one reason why, for instance, the president has put an emphasis on exports. He wants to double exports over the next five years. The reason there is when you have something like what they call a balance sheet recession, which means that people enter the recession in debt. So much of the stimulus that you try to provide ends up getting saved or spent just to pay down debt rather than buy new things. So in that sort of economy that doesn't have a lot of froth, you need an injection of money from somewhere else and the best way to do that is to sell goods that we make here overseas and then that money sort of, that money powers the recovery. So we don't necessarily want to have the same dependence on consumption. We want more stable growth. But still, you know, you still are going to have a situation where consumption is going to provide about two-thirds of your",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_10",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The speaker wants to revisit a previous point.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The group desires to find more stable sources of economic growth.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "A 'balance sheet recession' occurs when individuals enter a recession already in debt.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The president has emphasized increasing exports as part of economic strategy.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "In a balance sheet recession, fiscal stimulus tends to be saved or used to repay debt instead of stimulating demand.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The goal is to double exports within five years.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "In economies without significant speculative activity ('froth'), external injections of money are necessary for recovery.",
        "confidence": 0.91
