      },
      {
        "text": "In China, consumption primarily refers to basic needs such as shelter, communication, clothing, education, and healthcare.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "A key indicator of improved domestic demand in China would be lower savings rates and higher consumption.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "There is limited empirical evidence indicating a rise in China's consumption levels.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "It is unclear whether consumption in China is increasing significantly.",
