        "text": "The United States historically adopted universal high school education while much of Europe did not.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Education is the single best predictor of economic growth.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "South Korea and China have achieved substantial economic growth due in part to widespread education.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Universal high school education contributed significantly to America's superior economic performance relative to Europe over the past century.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "A more literate workforce can follow instructions and improve productivity in factories.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "There is currently a renewed national debate about whether all individuals should pursue college education.",
